Given a directed graph $G=(\mu, R)$, we say that  $G$ is realized as  an Ext-graph of
groups, provided that there exists a family of groups  $\{\mathbb G_\alpha: \alpha < \mu\}$  such
that for each $\alpha,\beta\in\mu$
\begin{center}
 $ {\rm Ext}(\mathbb G_\alpha,\mathbb G_\beta) = 0$ iff $ (\alpha,\beta) \in R$.
 \end{center}

